    [
      "heading",
      2,
      "result-and-persistence",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Result and persistence"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "DD mode performs a raw image write and copies the ISO layout to the whole target device. ISO mode formats a filesystem and extracts the ISO contents to create file-based live media. Neither mode is a MiniOS Installer deployment, and Rufus does not automatically create an ext4 partition or a persistence session."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Persistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/configuration/Boot-Modes.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Boot modes"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/configuration/Initrd-Persistence.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Initrd persistence"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " before relying on saved changes."
        ]
      ]
    ]
  ],
  "plain_text": "Using Rufus (Windows)\nRufus is a popular utility for Windows that helps format and create bootable USB drives.\nImportant\nWarning: Incorrect device selection will result in data loss! Always double-check the selected drive and backup important data.\nDrive Requirements\nDrive Size\nSee Hardware Compatibility Guide for detailed system requirements and drive sizes.\nInstalling Rufus\nDownload Rufus from the official website\nRun the program - Rufus doesn't require installation, it's a portable application\nCreating Bootable USB Drive\nRufus offers two methods for writing MiniOS to a USB drive:\nMethod 1: DD Mode (Recommended)\nLaunch Rufus as administrator\nSelect the USB drive in the \"Device\" field\nSelect the MiniOS ISO file:\nClick the \"SELECT\" button\nFind and select the downloaded MiniOS ISO file\nChoose write mode:\nIn the \"Hybrid ISO image detected\" dialog, select \"Write in DD Image mode\"\nStart the process: Click the \"START\" button\nConfirm the action - all data on the drive will be deleted\nWait for completion of the writing process\nMethod 2: ISO Mode (Alternative)\nLaunch Rufus as administrator\nSelect the USB drive in the \"Device\" field\nSelect the MiniOS ISO file:\nClick the \"SELECT\" button\nFind and select the downloaded MiniOS ISO file\nChoose write mode:\nIn the \"Hybrid ISO image detected\" dialog, select \"Write in ISO Image mode\"\nConfigure settings:\nFile system: FAT32 (recommended) or NTFS\nWhen choosing NTFS: EFI mode booting may be unavailable\nStart the process: Click the \"START\" button\nConfirm formatting - all data on the drive will be deleted\nResult and persistence\nDD mode performs a raw image write and copies the ISO layout to the whole target device. ISO mode formats a filesystem and extracts the ISO contents to create file-based live media. Neither mode is a MiniOS Installer deployment, and Rufus does not automatically create an ext4 partition or a persistence session.\nPersistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See Boot modes and Initrd persistence before relying on saved changes.",
  "product_kind": "minios-markup-document",
  "schema_version": 1
}
